  "body": "## Problem\n\nA sub2api deployment can sell a plan that is **shared out by shares** rather than by dollars: a key on it has no dollar cap, only a share of each 5-hour / 7-day window. Its `/v1/usage` can only report that through `rate_limits` as `used` of `limit: 100`.\n\nmagpie reads every `rate_limits` window as dollars (`readSub2APIKeyLimits` sets `Unit: \"USD\"`), so with the Balance URL set to such a key's `/v1/usage`:\n\n- the card says **`37.5 / 100 USD`**, though the key has spent no money;\n- *Check balance* / `magpie provider show` say **`$20.00`** (`Balance` takes `Limit - Amount`).\n\n## Proposal\n\nLet a window say it is a share: `\"unit\": \"percent\"` on a `rate_limits` entry.\n\n- Such a window is read as the share used alone (`Used`), with no `Amount` / `Limit` / `Unit`, so `Count` says nothing, as a subscription's window does. Name, span and `reset_at` are kept.\n- `Balance` gives the share the fullest window has left, e.g. `20%` (new `windowsLeft`).\n- A window with no `unit`, `\"USD\"` or anything else reads exactly as today. Routing (`KeyAllowance`) is unchanged, since it already goes by `Used`.\n\nExample reply:\n\n```json\n{\"mode\":\"unrestricted\",\"rate_limits\":[\n  {\"window\":\"5h\",\"limit\":100,\"used\":37.5,\"remaining\":62.5,\"unit\":\"percent\",\"reset_at\":\"2026-10-21T18:00:00Z\"},\n  {\"window\":\"7d\",\"limit\":100,\"used\":80,\"remaining\":20,\"unit\":\"percent\",\"reset_at\":\"2026-10-25T00:00:00Z\"}]}\n```\n\n## Patch (ready, since PRs from outside are closed)\n\nBranch: https://github.com/wtj-0527/magpie/tree/sub2api-percent-windows\nCommit: https://github.com/wtj-0527/magpie/commit/c7db44bc57a4f0535e9c8bf57a9e966059816fc1 (on `f5b0157`; touches `sub2api_usage.go`, `balance.go`, its test and fixture, and the \"A key's own windows\" row of `docs/subsystems/providers-accounts.md`).\n\n**Verification:**\n\n- `TestSub2APIKeySharesAreNotDollars` fails without the change with `5 hours = {... Amount:37.5 Limit:100 Unit:USD ...}`, and passes with it. It also checks `Balance` through httptest: `\"20%\"`.\n- `TestReadSub2APIKeyLimits`, `TestSub2APIKeyLimitsOnItsCard`, `TestKeyAllowance*` pass unchanged.\n- All runs under a temporary HOME with Go's caches pinned. `gofmt -l` is clean.\n- `GOOS=linux go vet -tags nogui ./...`, `GOOS=windows go vet ./...`, `GOOS=windows go build` and `GOOS=linux go build -tags nogui` pass.\n- `go test -tags nogui ./...` passes except `internal/agent` `TestAside{PostReadFailuresNeverOfferOffline,OfflineWriteFailureRollsBack,DisconnectUnavailableOnlyAtInitialRead,OfflineProviderWriteFailureRollsBackAllFiles}` and `internal/cli` `TestKeyNote`.\n  - Those fail identically on unmodified `f5b0157` on my machine, which runs as root in a container: chmod-based write refusals don't refuse, and `TestKeyNote` sees a container.\n- **Not run:** `go vet ./...` / `go build` without `nogui` (no fontconfig here), macOS.\n\nA related, separate proposal: an import link `balance=` parameter (#3187).\n",
